  "encodings": "Bytes and hashes are lowercase hex. signedText is UTF-8: chain tag, network id (hex of the block-0 hash; a label here), \"|\", then the kind's body; the wallet signs it with ML-DSA-65 (raw 3309-byte signature, 1952-byte key, both hex on the JSON routes). canonicalBytes: V1 = bincode of the transaction with hash, signatures and keys cleared; V2 = u64le 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF | u8 2 | the V1 preimage | u64le valid_until. hash = hex(SHA3-256(canonicalBytes)). wire = bincode with the same marker and version in front and valid_until at the end. dilithium_signature holds 4 placeholder bytes.",
